Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Gap-fused fmadd across Load/GEP windows (audited levkropp
 2e57bcf2 port)

Mul;[Load/GEP x1-2];Add chains now fuse into one fmadd emitted AT the
Add (nbody's j-side velocity updates: the constant GEP and velocity
load sit between fmul and fadd, so adjacent-only fusion never fired).
Both backends benefit through the shared emit_fused_mul_add hook:
nbody fmadd count 27 -> 45 on AArch64 AND x86-64; measured -6.8%
wall-clock on native x86 nbody (interleaved best-of-5; his AArch64
number was -3.3%). CCC_NO_GAP_FMA disables.

Audit findings vs his commit, fixed in this port:
- HIS ALIAS CHECK WAS INCOMPLETE: he rejected only gap destinations
  whose PHYSICAL REGISTER aliases a multiply operand's register. A gap
  destination can also alias a slot-homed operand's STACK SLOT: the
  multiply operands are read later than IR liveness recorded, and
  Tier-2 slot coloring may legally pack a gap-born value into the slot
  of a value whose liveness ended at the Mul. This port rejects both
  hazard classes (register AND slot identity, the latter only when the
  operand has no register home and will actually be reloaded).
- Accumulator gate wired to the same set as the fmsub gate (his commit
  predates our shared accumulator_dests; identical policy, one source
  of truth).
- Detector returns (mul_idx, add_idx) only -- the gap indices he
  returned were recomputed by his driver anyway; the driver here walks
  mul_idx+1..add_idx directly (no per-candidate Vec allocation).
- Disjointness with detect_mul_add_fusions is structural: that scan
  breaks at Load/GEP, this one breaks at Copy/Cast, so no Add can be
  claimed twice and no double-emission is possible.
- His debug-env eprintln paths dropped (CCC_DEBUG_GAPFMA), his
  gap-vector clone dropped.

Validation: 1073/1073 unit, 50/50 correctness, x86 regression 397/398
(1 = documented pre-existing check_tier2), ARM regression fail-set
identical to baseline (0 new), fuzz 300/300 x86-64 + 300/300 m32
O0-O2 + 300/300 aarch64 O1/O2/Os, ARM benchmark battery 8/8
output-identical vs gcc, nbody output bit-identical with fusion on/off
at both contract settings.
