Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Complete-unroll: extend trip bound to 16 under a
 512-instruction budget

Adopts the LIMITS of levkropp 1b4bac8b's full unroller (trip <= 16,
<= 512 expanded instructions) without adopting his separate 950-line
full_unroll_* machinery: our two-block complete unroller
(try_complete_unroll_two_block) already handles loop-carried phi
chaining and IV substitution; it was only artificially capped at
trip 8. His other 1b4bac8b half (try_hoist_def_chain terminal-def
fix) is already covered by our aggregate_copy_forward GEP hoist
(parallel evolution, verified line-by-line this session).

Budget gate: body_insts * trip <= 512, checked BEFORE cloning, using
saturating_mul (no overflow UB on adversarial trip counts). The
existing F32-only pow2 restriction and bit-iteration/call/asm/intrinsic
rejections stay untouched. Trip-12 dot-product kernel now fully
unrolls (0 branches) and computes identically to gcc.

Validation: 1073/1073 unit, 50/50 correctness, x86 regression 397/398
(1 = documented pre-existing check_tier2), ARM regression fail-set
unchanged, fuzz 300/300 x3 (x86-64 O1/O2, m32 O0-O2, aarch64
O1/O2/Os), benchmark battery geomean 1.377x vs gcc recorded as the
session baseline (struct_copy 1.58x, nbody 2.98x -- nbody is the
known FP-regalloc gap, tracked in BACKLOG).
